   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the town of Yorktown, county of Westchester, to alienate\nand discontinue the use of certain parklands",
    "basePrintNo": "S9212",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9212-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9212\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing the town of Yorktown, county of Westchester, to\nalienate and discontinue the use of certain parklands\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAuthorizes the town of Yorktown, county of Westchester, to alienate and\ndiscontinue the use of certain parklands\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Authorizes Yorktown to discontinue the use as parkland and\nalienate the lands described in the bill.\n\nSection 2 - Require Yorktown to dedicate an amount equal to or greater\nthan the fair market value of the parkland being alienated towards the\nacquisition of new parkland and/or capital improvements to existing park\nand recreational facilities.\n\nSection 3 - Provides the legal description of the land.\n\nSection 4 - If the town received federal money for the purchase, mainte-\nnance, or improvement of the parklands, the discontinuance and alien-\nation of such parkland shall not occur until the town has complied with\nany federal requirements.\n\nSection 5 - Effective Date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe town of Yorktown has requested this bill in compliance with the\nstate's rules regarding home rule.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
